  "system": "You review Python code for object-level authorization (access control on a specific object).\nYou are given an access policy, the name of a target function, and some source code.\nDecide whether the target function, as written, lets a requester obtain or disclose an object's data in a way the policy forbids.\n\nRules:\n- Judge only from the code shown. Do not assume authorization logic that is not visible.\n- An `if` statement, or a name containing words such as \"owner\", \"check\", \"guard\" or \"auth\", is not evidence by itself. Confirm what is actually compared, with which values, and what happens when the comparison fails.\n- A call whose return value is ignored does not block anything unless the called code itself raises or stops execution.\n- Data that is returned, yielded, written, appended or sent before a failing check has already been disclosed.\n- If deciding requires code that is not shown (for example a called function whose body is missing), answer \"insufficient_context\" and name what is missing.\n- If the policy allows the access, it is not a problem.\n\nVerdict values:\n- \"vulnerable\": the visible code lets a requester access or disclose data against the policy.\n- \"no_issue_found\": the visible code enforces the policy for the target function.\n- \"insufficient_context\": the decision depends on code that is not shown.\n\nReply with JSON only: {\"verdict\": ..., \"evidence\": ..., \"missing_context\": [...]}.\n\"evidence\" quotes the relevant code lines and explains them briefly. \"missing_context\" lists the missing information (empty list if none).",
  "prompt": "ACCESS POLICY:\nAn appointment may be viewed or changed only by the users who take part in it (its student or its professor).\n\nENDPOINT: PATCH /appointments/{appointment_id}\nTARGET FUNCTION: app.routers.resources.patch_appointment (the handler of this endpoint)\n\nCODE:\n```python\n# file: app/database.py\ndef get_db():\n    db = SessionLocal()\n    try:\n        yield db\n    finally:\n        db.close()\n\n# file: app/dependencies.py\ndef get_appointment_for_user(appointment_id: str, current_user: User=Depends(get_current_user), db: Session=Depends(get_db)) -> Appointment:\n    appointment = db.get(Appointment, appointment_id)\n    if appointment is None:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail='Appointment not found')\n    return appointment\n\n# file: app/routers/resources.py\n@router.patch('/appointments/{appointment_id}', response_model=AppointmentOut)\ndef patch_appointment(payload: AppointmentUpdate, appointment: Appointment=Depends(get_appointment_for_user), db: Session=Depends(get_db)):\n    for field, value in payload.model_dump(exclude_unset=True).items():\n        setattr(appointment, field, value)\n    db.commit()\n    db.refresh(appointment)\n    return appointment\n```\n\nCONTEXT NOTE:\nOnly selected functions from the codebase are shown. Classes (including data models and schemas) and module-level variables are not shown.\nCalls not shown:\n- app.auth.get_current_user(...): defined in this codebase but not shown (call depth limit)\n- SessionLocal(...) called in app.database.get_db: not resolved by the extractor (module_variable), body not shown\n- db.close(...) called in app.database.get_db: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- db.get(...) called in app.dependencies.get_appointment_for_user: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- HTTPException(...) called in app.dependencies.get_appointment_for_user: not resolved by the extractor (imported), body not shown\n- payload.model_dump(exclude_unset=True).items(...) called in app.routers.resources.patch_appointment: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- payload.model_dump(...) called in app.routers.resources.patch_appointment: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- db.commit(...) called in app.routers.resources.patch_appointment: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- db.refresh(...) called in app.routers.resources.patch_appointment: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n\nReturn the JSON object.",
